# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
# `.env` is git-ignored — never commit real credentials.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Contact form submission endpoint. The site is fully static, so
# no server secret ever ships to the browser. Recommended options:
#   1. https://api.web3forms.com/submit  (free, public access-key by design)
#   2. A Cloudflare Worker you own, proxying to Telegram/email server-side
# Either way: never put a bot token or private API key directly in
# frontend source — that is exactly the pattern this rebuild removes.
PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://api.web3forms.com/submit
PUBLIC_FORM_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-your-public-access-key
